# MIDAS Obsidian vault — this documentation IS version-controlled.
#
# `docs/*` above — not a bare `docs/` — is what makes this work. Git cannot re-include
# a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is ignored, so a bare `docs/` silently kills every
# negation below it no matter where they sit. Excluding children one at a time leaves
# a child available to be un-excluded. Same idiom as the midas-deploy block below.
#
# Only `*.md` needs an explicit negation: line 95's bare `*.md` is the sole ignore rule
# that matches vault content. Everything else under the vault (.base, .svg) becomes
# trackable the moment the directory itself stops being excluded.
#
# Still ignored, deliberately: docs/_archive/, docs/.obsidian/, and any loose file at
# the top level of docs/. Generated .claude-flow/ state inside the vault stays ignored
# by the bare rule at the very end of this file — which must remain last.
docs/MIDAS-Vault/
docs/MIDAS-Vault/**/*.md
docs/MIDAS-Vault/**/*.base

# midas-deploy skill — this IS version-controlled.
# Overrides `.claude/` (line 9) and the bare `*.md` rule (line 95). Unlike the
# vault rules above, a parent directory is excluded here, and git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is ignored — so every level must be
# un-excluded in turn before the leaf negation can take effect.
.claude/
.claude/*
.claude/skills/
.claude/skills/*
.claude/skills/midas-deploy/
.claude/skills/midas-deploy/**

# Generated agent-runtime state (neural/*.json, policy/state.json), rewritten on
# every session and never source. Bare pattern, so it matches at any depth — the
# 12 copies scattered through backend/, frontend/src/**, docs/ and .claude/.
# Must stay last: it has to win over the midas-deploy negation directly above.
.claude-flow/
